<title>FRANCE: Firemen put out southern France forest fire.</title>
<headline>Firemen put out southern France forest fire.</headline>
<dateline>BORDEAUX, France 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Firemen backed by aircraft put out a forest fire early on Sunday which destroyed 700 hectares (1,750 acres) of pines near the southwestern French town of Bordeaux.</p>
<p>The blaze, apparently started by a car accident, destroyed two fire engines but no-one was injured and there was no damage to property, firemen said.</p>
<p>Drought and unseasonally high temperatures have raised fears of forest fires across southern France.</p>
